{
  "title": "scTWAS in colorectal cancer: analysis code, curated peak sets and trained GReX models",
  "description": "<p>Code and resources accompanying <em>Single-cell transcriptome-wide association study in colorectal cancer</em>. The analysis covers cell-type reference construction and cis-eQTL mapping, accessible-chromatin peak calling, GReX model training, S-PrediXcan association testing, colocalization and SMR-HEIDI, TF networks, multi-omics support, drug-target annotation, iLINCS connectivity, DepMap dependency, and arrayed CRISPR-Cas9 viability. The code also covers follow-up of CRC GWAS lead variants and manuscript figure rendering.</p><p>See the article's Data availability statement for access to the trained GReX models, chromatin peak sets, GWAS summary statistics, and individual-level cohort data. The repository README describes the workflow and archive inputs.</p>",
